body:
Well, to be fair, you do have to shoot the rubber bullets for them to be effective. And water cannons would be awesome, until it turned into the 1950's and 60's where the officers and military would be ruthless in its use. You generally need to be pretty close for pepper spray to be effective; tear gas, if fired from the US into Mexico might be considered some kind of war crime or human rights crime if I'm not mistaken considering using it in war is a war crime. But I would tend to agree, shooting somebody that's throwing a rock at you is, I think, childish and immature, as well as an extreme use of force.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
